+# Serve agent tools over MCP from the existing routes
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with their own AI assistants and want them to search the
+blog and draft posts. We do not want a chatbot in the blog, a second
+implementation of search or of post creation, or protocol code of our
+own to maintain.
+
+## Decision
+
+Two existing routes declare `agent` metadata in `routes/web.ts` and are
+served as MCP tools by `@guren/plugin-mcp` at `POST /mcp`:
+
+| Tool | Route | Read-only |
+|---|---|---|
+| `posts_search` | `QUERY /posts/search` (`posts.search`) | yes |
+| `posts_store` | `POST /posts` (`posts.store`) | no |
+
+- A tool call re-enters the app as the route's own HTTP request, so the
+  `auth` middleware, the route's body schema and `PostPolicy` decide it
+  exactly as they do for the website. There is no tool class.
+- Tool names use underscores (`agent.toolName`): some assistants drop
+  names outside `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`. Route names are unchanged.
+- `posts_store` declares no hints. Read-only is derived from the HTTP
+  method, and the default for a writing tool ("may be destructive") is
+  what makes an assistant ask its user first.
+- Credentials are the framework's API tokens, kept hashed in the
+  `api_tokens` table through `DatabaseApiTokenStore` (`src/app.ts`).
+  A bearer request is authenticated as the token's user; the author of a
+  created post is that user, never a value from the input.
+- Which tools a credential reaches is its scopes (`tools:read`,
+  `tool:posts_store`, `tools:*`). Ops issue one from a terminal:
+
+  ```bash
+  bunx guren token:issue --name "Ada's assistant" --user 1 --tools tools:read
+  ```
+
+- A token opens nothing but its tools. Accepting bearers makes every
+  route authenticate them, where no scope is checked, so
+  `ConfineApiTokensMiddleware` wraps all routes and refuses (403) a
+  token on any route that is not an agent tool its scopes grant.
+
+- `PostController.store` answers a caller asking for JSON with the
+  created post (201) instead of the redirect the form follows, because
+  an assistant has no page to land on.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A change to the search or to the post rules reaches assistants with no
+  further work, and `bunx guren tool:list` shows what is exposed.
+- Exposing another route is a decision, not a default: it needs its own
+  `agent` metadata, and `bunx guren check` fails a writing tool whose
+  action does not authorize.
+- Rate limits are the plugin's defaults and are kept per process.
+- There is no page for users to manage their credentials, no approval
+  queue and no audit sink yet.
